  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nResearch construction and sharp boundary cost; no new kappa. Fixed children\n`C_i(D,W)=(D+R_i W,-W)` can keep their readers unchanged while the parent\nnegates the smaller output between calls. The exact uniform boundary minimum\nis `(k mod 2)N + 2 floor(k/2) min(N,d)` in the declared complete-register\nnegation alphabet. A full two-pass dirty echo makes the returned output depend\nonly on the source and restores all incoming scratch.\n\nThe seed-selected five-child, width-eight, one-output example uses **200\nscalar instructions versus 256 eager**, saving 56 negations. The package\nincludes the written proof, recursive ADD/NEG and storage recurrences, source\ncopies, both child directions, data accesses, descriptor reads and preparation\ncharges. All ten added files are in `research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/`.\n\n**The child boundary is a real restriction.** A compiler allowed to rewrite\ninside the explicit matrix leaves can beat both words. No optimal matrix\nalgorithm, physical supplier, runtime gain, tape realization, rounding theorem,\nor complete multiplication proof is claimed. Intermediate observers also need\nan additional priced interface because the physical output can be negated.\n\n[Proof and scope](https://github.com/thakrarsagar/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f39574ae9b2e3cceb01e29cf48e134f409ec1b0f/research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/README.md) \u00b7\n[Exact certificate](https://github.com/thakrarsagar/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f39574ae9b2e3cceb01e29cf48e134f409ec1b0f/research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/CERTIFICATE.json) \u00b7\n[Source pins](https://github.com/thakrarsagar/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f39574ae9b2e3cceb01e29cf48e134f409ec1b0f/research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/SOURCE-PINS.json)\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nThe user's recursive-interface assignment was refined to this exact immutable\nreader contract. OS-random assignment seed **51**; local claim made within the\nfirst eight minutes. No scope change after the claim and no pivot.\n\nInvestigation base: `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`. The final fetch\nfound upstream `49b3157d1d89adcef16df8be98445451672be5ba`, with unchanged selected\nPR1094 evidence. Its new submission guidance was inspected. This standalone\narchive format retains its own exact replay and source pins, rather than\ninventing a catalogue assignment for the user's explicit track.\n\nNearest predecessors are #1155 at `9821c6e9388f3fc097e94b72be9fa7b41a849527`,\n#1199 at `85ac2880ea5bda44f28632b71ffa2b4e35ec6b7d`, #1203 at\n`38459854fd5bb93099871a84324413bd0e338d8e`, and #1205 at\n`e2008d7ffcad464da7ec21c69e8d8a8c91de4930`. Compatible nonzero readers and\nobserver distinctions are already their results. This package adds paid\noutput sign changes, the sharp uniform boundary count, and a recursively\nexecutable source-only echo. It does not claim priority for dirty echo\ncancellation, which also appears in #889.\n\nImmediately before submission, checked 834 open PRs through #1225. The broad\nkeyword match #784 optimizes leaf-call counts for ordered echo trees, a\ndifferent object. #1211 prices balanced factor-tape travel; #1216 excludes\ncheap restored CK/JP8 donors. No matching wrapper was found. All five current\ndiscussions were checked; no pinned sprint issue existed, so the claim is local.\nThis is bounded overlap evidence, not proof of novelty.\n\n## Validation\n\nStandard library only. From the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_OUTPUT_SIGN_RESTORATION ... saved_NEG=56 source_pins=3 kappa=unchanged`\nand `PASS_OUTPUT_SIGN_PACKAGE relocation=1 corruptions=4`.\n\nPassed with CPython 3.14.8 in normal and optimized mode and CPython 3.11.17\nin optimized mode. Evidence includes all 21,840 gap schedules through six\nchildren, 384 exact price comparisons, 384 recursive cases on all 3,168 basis\ncolumns, literal inverses, rational dirty probes, depth-two/three dense cases,\nseven mathematical controls and seven invalid-input controls. The standalone\npackage test rejects four real on-disk corruptions. Certificate regeneration\nis byte-identical; all retained source hashes and base-context hashes match.\n\nThese are finite implementation checks alongside the written general proof,\nnot formal verification of the full multiplication theorem. The selected cold\nreplay, Linux execution and human peer review were not run. Hosted CI status\nmust be assessed separately. No selected construction or upstream file changed.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe [next question](https://github.com/thakrarsagar/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f39574ae9b2e3cceb01e29cf48e134f409ec1b0f/research/output-sign-restoration-seed51/README.md#open-next-questions)\nis whether a supported supplier has an indivisible sign-drifting child with\nfewer outputs than workspace coordinates. First trace one candidate's complete\nsource-return map and retained boundary, then price routing and precision. No\nsuch supplier has been identified here. If its terminal negation can simply be\nremoved, reject that candidate immediately.\n\n## Credit\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in algebra,\nimplementation, verification and writing. Credits Aaron Wang / navinor for\n#1155, Sagar Thakrar for #1199, mightyOil for #1203, Adam Gall for #1205, and\nCubeJerry for #889. Three predecessor notes are retained byte-for-byte with\ntheir notices; no predecessor implementation is imported. New material is\nApache-2.0 under the repository license. The selected Rohan Arun / Jeremy Kothe\nconstruction and its earlier contributor chain remain unchanged.\n",
